%% 5.4 Team submission → validation → fixture generation
%% Source of truth for this diagram. Rendered from ../specs/2026-08-03-events-feature-spec.md §5.4
%% Edit here, not in the spec — the spec links to this file.
sequenceDiagram
    actor O as Organizer (mobile)
    participant API as Events API
    participant DB as MongoDB
    participant CH as Chat
    participant N as Notifications

    Note over O: the client performs the shuffle<br/>and finalizes the teams

    alt client-submitted teams (default)
        O->>API: PUT /events/:id/teams { teams:[{name, playerIds}] }
        API->>API: assert organizer + status == 'preparation'
        API->>DB: load joined EventPlayers
        API->>API: validate — ids joined, no player in two teams,<br/>no dupes, names unique, 2..6 teams
        alt validation fails
            API-->>O: 400 naming the offending id
        end
    else server-side shuffle (fallback)
        O->>API: POST /events/:id/shuffle
        API->>API: assert organizer + status == 'preparation'
        API->>DB: load joined EventPlayers
        API->>API: Fisher-Yates → deal across teamCount colours
    end

    Note over API,DB: both paths converge below

    API->>DB: bulkWrite EventPlayer.team<br/>(clear team on players dropped from the roster)
    API->>API: double round-robin over the finalized teams
    Note over API: leg 1 (i,j) then leg 2 (j,i)<br/>N=4 → 12 matches, 6 per team
    API->>DB: replace EventMatch rows for this event<br/>(delete then insert — all scores null)
    API->>CH: upsert EventTeamChat per team name
    API->>N: notify each assigned player of their team
    API-->>O: { teams, fixtures, unassignedPlayerIds }

    Note over O: unassignedPlayerIds lets the app warn<br/>"3 players not on a team" — partial rosters are allowed

    opt resubmit while still in preparation
        O->>API: PUT /events/:id/teams (revised)
        API->>DB: teams AND fixtures regenerated
        Note over API,DB: safe — scores cannot exist yet<br/>(entry requires 'playing')
    end
